      "sourceTextSha256": "09d465ce4f75f5dcad7244924ad139427847dff1bd44701717cf783a28a49f14",
      "text": "Day 8 · Sail to the Maroon village of Nieuw-Aurora for a walk past the mission post, church, school and medical post, and hear about the Maroons, descendants of Africans who escaped slavery, and their traditions; walk in the island’s forest to learn about medicinal plants, with dinner and a cultural dance performance in the evening (minimum 8 guests). The next morning, swim, walk or revisit the village before lunch, then return by boat to Atjoni and by bus to Paramaribo.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
